<article class="env-remark" id="053V">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/053V">Remark <span data-tag="053V">37.52.5</span>.</a> The proof of Lemma <a href="/tag/053U" data-tag="053U">37.52.4</a> actually shows that there exists a sequence of specializations </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  x \leadsto x_1 \leadsto x_2 \leadsto \ldots \leadsto x_ d \leadsto x'  \]
</div>
  <p> where all $x_ i$ are in the fibre $X_ s$, each specialization is immediate, and $x_ d$ is a closed point of $X_ s$. The integer $d = \text{trdeg}_{\kappa (s)}(\kappa (x)) = \dim (\overline{\{ x\} })$ where the closure is taken in $X_ s$. Moreover, the points $x_ i$ can be chosen to avoid any closed subset of $X_ s$ which does not contain the point $x$. </p>
</article>